  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "An enzyme's activity depends on general conditions, such as temperature and pH, and on chemicals that act on it specifically."
   ],
   [
    7.747,
    "Every enzyme has an optimal temperature, where its shape is the most active."
   ],
   [
    12.552,
    "For a typical human enzyme, that is about thirty seven degrees Celsius."
   ],
   [
    17.122,
    "An enzyme from heat tolerant bacteria, living in hot springs, peaks near seventy seven degrees Celsius."
   ],
   [
    24.18,
    "Cooler than the optimum, the molecules move slowly, so the rate falls."
   ],
   [
    28.88,
    "Hotter, and the shape unravels."
   ],
   [
    31.354,
    "The enzyme is denatured, and the rate crashes to almost nothing."
   ],
   [
    35.677,
    "Notice that the human enzyme has stopped by about fifty degrees, while the bacterial one is still running."
   ],
   [
    41.797,
    "That is one reason a very high fever is dangerous: some of the body's enzymes begin to lose their shape."
   ]
  ]
 },
