    0.104,
    "Some enzymes need a helper."
   ],
   [
    1.797,
    "Cofactors are nonprotein enzyme helpers."
   ],
   [
    4.909,
    "Some are inorganic, such as a metal ion like zinc or iron."
   ],
   [
    9.167,
    "An organic cofactor is called a coenzyme, and many coenzymes are made from vitamins."
   ],
   [
    14.805,
    "Without its helper, the enzyme cannot do its job."
   ],
   [
    18.06,
    "Many enzymes hold a zinc or an iron ion right in the active site, where it helps grip the substrate."
   ],
   [
    24.648,
    "That is one reason we need small amounts of these minerals, and of vitamins, in our diet."
   ]
  ]
